config HAVE_AVM_RTE
	bool

config AVM_RTE
	bool "AVM real-time enhancements"
	depends on HAVE_AVM_RTE
	default y
	help
	 The AVM real-time enhancement (RTE) framework allows executing
	 code with low-latency requirements in high-priority interrupt
	 handlers.  On ARM, these are Fast Interrupts, on MIPS, they execute
	 as yield threads.
	 One prominent user of this is the AVM telephony stack.
